Sun Microsystems / Oracle
-------------------------
The OpenSPARC T1 and T2 source release: the hypervisor and OpenBoot in
src/, kept as published in OpenSPARCT2_Arch.1.2.tar.bz2 file
(PRISTINE-MANIFEST says what was removed).

OpenSPARC T1:
    https://www.oracle.com/servers/technologies/opensparc-t1-page.html

OpenSPARC T2:
    https://www.oracle.com/servers/technologies/opensparc-t2-page.html

T2 archive, the source of src/:
    https://download.oracle.com/technetwork/systems/opensparc/OpenSPARCT2_Arch.1.2.tar.bz2

T1 archive, with the Solaris 10 Legion disk image (S10image/disk.s10hw2):
    https://download.oracle.com/technetwork/systems/opensparc/OpenSPARCT1_Arch.1.5.tar.bz2
    (hashes of both archives: tests/full/md/expected/sun-archives.sha256)

Project Q (sun4v), Sun's architecture specifications and FWARC list:
    https://sun4v.github.io/
    (the archive of the closed Kenai.com site)

Artyom Tarasenko
----------------
The niagara machine in QEMU (-M niagara, hw/sparc64/niagara.c), which every
machine here runs on.

qemu-sun4v-md, a ready-made 1 GiB MD and firmware set for -M niagara:
    https://github.com/artyom-tarasenko/qemu-sun4v-md/tree/1GiB-experimental
    (directory 1GiB-snv_77, an independent reference for the MDs here)

hsimd, Sun's driver files published unchanged as a repository:
    https://github.com/artyom-tarasenko/hsimd

illumos (the open source descendant of OpenSolaris)
---------------------------------------------------
The OpenSolaris code on which illumos is based is the only guaranteed,
confirmed way to validate that the components of sun4v-qemu-kit work.

illumos-gate:
    https://github.com/illumos/illumos-gate

SPARC Compliance Definition 2.4.1 (SPARC International, 1999), section 3P-8,
the stack frame that stack.h implements:
    https://sparc.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/SCD.2.4.1.pdf.gz

